# cellpose pipeline

First, you can setup a dedicated conda environment. Inside the current directory, 
use:
```
conda env create -f environment.yml
conda activate ads-cellpose
```

## Data
The data we use for finetuning is the Stanford SRF dataset, available here: 
https://doi.org/10.48324/dandi.001350/0.250511.1527

The SRF testing set is available on github: https://github.com/axondeepseg/data_axondeepseg_srf_testing/archive/refs/tags/r20250513-neurips2025.zip

## Preprocess the data
The data is originally in BIDS format. Using the following script, we can 
preprocess the data by organizing it in a convenient format for the cellpose pipeline.
You should preprocess both the training and testing sets, like so:
```
python prepare_data <SRF_TRAIN_SET> -o cellpose_preprocessed/train
python prepare_data <SRF_TEST_SET> -o cellpose_preprocessed/test
```
By default, this will create 4 sets of image-mask pairs: for both the training 
and testing sets, there will be separate sets for myelinated and unmyelinated 
axons.